"The normal form of the counterexample to the maximin property in Section 9, giving Player 1's
expected payoff (Player 2 receives the negative). A strategy y<n><t> of Player 1 plays y<n> if
Player 1 is in class a1 and y<t> if in a2; a strategy z<u><v> of Player 2 plays z<u> if in b1 and
z<v> if in b2. The only saddle point is (y11,z11), with value 0."

